WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.940
Push a tiny bead into a chick embryo's forebrain.

2
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.780
The bead is soaked in one protein, FGF8.

3
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.480
A second midbrain can grow there, built back to front.

4
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.480
How can one bead do that?

5
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.760
Cells in the neural tube must know where they sit.

6
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.460
Who tells them?

7
00:00:26.933 --> 00:00:31.293
Hox genes give the hindbrain and spinal cord their addresses.

8
00:00:31.733 --> 00:00:35.693
But the midbrain and forebrain have no Hox code at all.

9
00:00:36.293 --> 00:00:37.633
They need other instructions.

10
00:00:38.433 --> 00:00:39.433
Where do those come from?

11
00:00:39.953 --> 00:00:44.813
A local organizer is a small signaling center inside the neural tube.

12
00:00:45.253 --> 00:00:47.593
It tells the cells around it what to build.

13
00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:54.207
The best studied sits where the midbrain meets the hindbrain, at a narrowing called

14
00:00:54.207 --> 00:00:58.347
the isthmus. Two transcription factors draw the line.

15
00:00:59.427 --> 00:01:02.587
OTX2 is on in the forebrain and midbrain.

16
00:01:03.587 --> 00:01:06.467
GBX2 is on in the front of the hindbrain.

17
00:01:07.407 --> 00:01:11.027
Each represses the other, so the edge between them is sharp.

18
00:01:11.817 --> 00:01:16.917
At that line, a set of genes switches on and keeps itself going.

19
00:01:17.917 --> 00:01:21.557
FGF8 forms a band just behind the boundary.

20
00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:24.857
Wnt1 forms a ring just in front.

21
00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:29.957
Engrailed and Pax2 and Pax5 span the boundary.

22
00:01:30.777 --> 00:01:33.877
In the standard model, each helps keep the others on.

23
00:01:34.557 --> 00:01:36.477
Remove one, and the rest fade.

24
00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:39.167
Is that enough to organize?

25
00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:41.927
This tests sufficiency.

26
00:01:42.827 --> 00:01:45.607
Put an FGF8 bead in the forebrain.

27
00:01:46.707 --> 00:01:48.687
Cells next to it turn on Engrailed.

28
00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:51.347
Later they form a midbrain.

29
00:01:52.247 --> 00:01:54.487
The new midbrain is a mirror image.

30
00:01:55.407 --> 00:01:59.207
Parts that normally lie nearest the isthmus form nearest the bead.

31
00:02:00.107 --> 00:02:02.687
Parts from farther forward form farther away.

32
00:02:02.687 --> 00:02:07.287
That is what you expect if cells read their distance from a source.

33
00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:11.720
Now test necessity by removing the signal.

34
00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:17.820
Mouse embryos with no Wnt1 lack the midbrain and much of the cerebellum.

35
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.720
Mice that make greatly reduced FGF8 lose the midbrain and cerebellum too.

36
00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.680
Add a factor where it is absent, and the structure forms.

37
00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.140
Remove it, and the structure is lost.

38
00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.000
You need both tests.
